# 5.3.scenario.rerank.redteam.refine.stone

## .what

**refine** the ranks. weigh each survivor's steelman (5.1) against its attack (5.2), and settle the
red-teamed weight — the second, sharper probability pass over the coarse rank from phase 3. this is
the pass that decides which survivors earn deep research in phase 6.

## .inputs

- `5.1.scenario.rerank.redteam.steelman.yield.md` — the best case for each survivor
- `5.2.scenario.rerank.redteam.attack.yield.md` — the strongest case against each
- `3.3.scenario.disentangle.correlation.blend.yield.md` — the coarse rank + severity

## .do

- for each survivor, reconcile steelman vs attack into a **refined weight** — still ordinal, still
  bracketed (no false-precision midpoint)
- keep severity separate from probability: a low-probability branch that stays severe does not fall
  off — it stays live for the veto (`rule.require.superposition-until-elimination`)
- name the **survivor set that passes to phase 6** — the scenarios that earn deep research (bounds,
  prevention, care), plus every un-eliminated catastrophic branch regardless of rank

## .emit

into `5.3.scenario.rerank.redteam.refine.yield.md` — the refined-rank superposition + the phase-6
survivor set.

## .done when

every survivor has a refined ordinal weight, severity is kept distinct from probability, and the
phase-6 survivor set is named (all un-eliminated catastrophic branches included).
